course: dictionary
lesson: 13694
title: Words carved to last
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To inscribe something is to write, carve or engrave words or a design on it, such as stone, metal or a ring. «The names of the soldiers are inscribed on the monument.» A monument is built to last, so inscribe must mean cut or written in a way that lasts.
explain: You can also inscribe a book by writing a personal message in it. «She inscribed a kind message inside my birthday book.» The clues are birthday and kind message, so inscribe means writing something special for one person.
explain: In maths, to inscribe a shape means to draw it inside another shape so that it fits exactly and touches it. «A circle is inscribed in the square.» Ask: does the circle fit inside the square and touch every side? If it does, inscribed means fitted inside.
fact: Inscribe is a verb: inscribe, inscribes, inscribed, inscribing.
fact: «Inscribed» means written, carved or engraved on something.
fact: Phrases to know: inscribed on, inscribed with, inscribed circle.
fact: Trophies and rings are often inscribed with names or dates.
fact: An inscribed circle touches every side of the shape around it.
exercise: «The gold ring was inscribed with her name.» What does inscribed mean? | Hidden inside a box | Painted in red paint | Sold at the market | *Carved or engraved onto it
exercise: «He inscribed a kind message in my book.» What did he do? | Gave the book back | Read the book aloud | *Wrote a personal message in it | Lost the book
exercise: In maths, a circle is inscribed in a square. What does that mean? | *The circle is drawn inside the square, touching every side | The circle is painted on the back of the square | The circle is cut out of the square | The circle is bigger than the square
test: «The names of the heroes are inscribed on the memorial stone.» Which word means the same as inscribed? | Folded | *Engraved | Erased | Hidden
test: Which shape can be inscribed in a square so that it touches every side? | Triangle | Star | *Circle | Cross
exam: Which sentence uses inscribe correctly? | The artist inscribing is the painting corner | The artist inscribe her signature on the corner of the painting | *The artist inscribed her signature on the corner of the painting | The artist inscribes yesterday the painting
